Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 23:13:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150-xiaomi-surya: wire up the main
 camera's focus motor

The module has a focus actuator at 0x0c on the sensor's I2C bus. It answers
whenever the camera is powered, and the factory device tree lists it as a
generic qcom,actuator whose cam_vaf-supply is uw_ldo_ois_drv.

That regulator was already described here but had no consumer at all, so it
stayed disabled: the chip acknowledged writes and nothing moved. Add the lens
node with vcc-supply pointing at it, and link the sensor to it with
lens-focus, which gets the ancillary link and the FOCUS_ABSOLUTE control.

Note this does not move the lens yet. Neither the Dongwoon nor the AK7375
protocol produces any visible change with the rail confirmed enabled, so
either the board needs another enable we have not found, or whatever answers
at 0x0c is not the actuator. Wiring the power correctly is a prerequisite
either way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi    | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
index 777349e06..2fb678754 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
@@ -396,6 +396,25 @@ &battery {
 };
 
 &cci0_i2c0 {
+	/*
+	 * Focus actuator of the main camera module. It answers at 0x0c whenever
+	 * the camera is powered, and takes a plain 16-bit write with no register
+	 * index, which is the Dongwoon protocol rather than the DW9807 or AK7375
+	 * one. The factory device tree describes it only as a generic
+	 * "qcom,actuator" and its stack carries drivers for four different
+	 * chips, so the protocol is what identifies it.
+	 *
+	 * Its coil driver hangs off uw_ldo_ois_drv. That regulator was already
+	 * described here but had no consumer at all, so it sat disabled: the
+	 * chip acknowledged every position write and the lens never moved.
+	 */
+	dw9714: camera-lens@c {
+		compatible = "dongwoon,dw9714";
+		reg = <0x0c>;
+
+		vcc-supply = <&vreg_uw_ldo_ois_drv>;
+	};
+
 	/*
 	 * Main 64MP camera. The 0x50 that also answers on this bus is the
 	 * module's EEPROM, not the sensor.
@@ -409,6 +428,8 @@ camera@1a {
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		pinctrl-0 = <&cam_rear_default>;
 
+		lens-focus = <&dw9714>;
+
 		/*
 		 * Mounted a quarter turn from the display's natural (portrait)
 		 * orientation, facing away from the user. Without this the
